      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok that makes sense. but the part about \"unaided memory\" is what worries me. like, if i implement a specific algorithm i learned there, and someone asks how i knew to do it that way, i'm technically using my memory of it. where is the line between \"unaided memory\" and actually using their trade secrets? wouldn't they try to claim that most of the complex logic is theirs?",
